From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Gtk4: a batched ListBox item must not be created hidden

Comparing the sample on both engines showed Form2's list box rendering six
captioned rows on Gtk3 and, on Gtk4, a band of blank rows followed by only the
items appended at run time.

The blank rows were not a spacing problem: they had no visible caption. NativeAdd
and NativeInsert build each item's Gtk.Label with Visible = !IsUpdateing, on the
Gtk3 assumption that EndUpdate's ShowAll() would reveal it again - ShowAll was
recursive and walked into the rows. Gtk4 removed it, and its compatibility
replacement deliberately does not recurse (resurrecting descendants that were
hidden on purpose is the bug that got gtk_widget_show_all deleted), so
EndUpdate's Show() sets Visible on the list box and nothing else. Every caption
created inside a batch therefore stayed hidden for good - and because
ObjectCollection.AddRange wraps its whole batch in BeginUpdate/EndUpdate, that
silently covered every designer-declared item.

The caption is now created visible, which is Gtk4's own doctrine: a widget is
visible when it is created and hiding one is a deliberate act. There is no
flicker to suppress in exchange - Gtk4 renders nothing until the frame clock
ticks, so a batch of added rows is already coalesced into a single layout pass,
and all EndUpdate has left to do is ask for it.
diff --git a/Gtk.Windows.Forms/System/Windows/Forms/ListBox.cs b/Gtk.Windows.Forms/System/Windows/Forms/ListBox.cs
index 38c0fa38..588e7911 100644
--- a/Gtk.Windows.Forms/System/Windows/Forms/ListBox.cs
+++ b/Gtk.Windows.Forms/System/Windows/Forms/ListBox.cs
@@ -707,7 +707,11 @@ public partial class ListBox : ListControl
     public void EndUpdate()
     {
         IsUpdateing = false;
-        self.ListBox.Show();
+        // Gtk4 has no recursive show: the Gtk3 build ended a batch with ShowAll(), which walked the
+        // rows and revealed the captions it had created hidden. Its replacement only sets Visible on
+        // the widget it is called on, so nothing may be created hidden here (see NativeAdd) and all
+        // that is left to do is ask for the layout the batch made stale.
+        self.ListBox.QueueResize();
     }
 
     /// <summary>
@@ -993,7 +997,9 @@ public partial class ListBox : ListControl
         var row = new Gtk.ListBoxRow();
         row.HeightRequest = ItemHeight > 0 ? ItemHeight : DefaultItemHeight;
         row.Visible = true;
-        row.AddChild(new Gtk.Label(item.ToString()) { Valign = Align.Center, Halign = Align.Start, Hexpand = true, Vexpand = true, Visible = !IsUpdateing });
+        // The caption must be created visible even inside a BeginUpdate/EndUpdate batch: Gtk4 has no
+        // recursive show to reveal it again, so a row hidden here would stay blank for good.
+        row.AddChild(new Gtk.Label(item.ToString()) { Valign = Align.Center, Halign = Align.Start, Hexpand = true, Vexpand = true });
         self.ListBox.AddChild(row);
     }
 
@@ -1041,7 +1047,8 @@ public partial class ListBox : ListControl
         var row = new Gtk.ListBoxRow();
         row.HeightRequest = ItemHeight > 0 ? ItemHeight : DefaultItemHeight;
         row.Visible = true;
-        row.AddChild(new Gtk.Label(item.ToString()) { Valign = Align.Center, Halign = Align.Start, Hexpand = true, Vexpand = true, Visible = !IsUpdateing });
+        // Created visible for the same reason as NativeAdd - nothing reveals it later under Gtk4.
+        row.AddChild(new Gtk.Label(item.ToString()) { Valign = Align.Center, Halign = Align.Start, Hexpand = true, Vexpand = true });
         self.ListBox.Insert(row, index);
     }
 
